### Key Verification Summary

1. **Learning-Check Failure Path**:
   - In [`cf_ratio.py:802-823`](file:///home/u24/papers/mcrl-leo-handover-cf3/src/mcrl/algorithms/cf_ratio.py#L802-L823), when `LearningCheckStop` is raised at episode 500, `train_cf` catches it, sets `log["quarter"] = stop.row`, appends the completed episode log to `logs`, and executes `episode_callback(log)` before re-raising.
   - In [`run_cf3_pilot.py:355-362`](file:///home/u24/papers/mcrl-leo-handover-cf3/scripts/run_cf3_pilot.py#L355-L362), `save(len(logs))` writes `next_episode: 500`, `episodes_completed: 500`, and persists exactly 500 log rows to `episode-logs.json`. The previous `len(logs) + 1` synthesis defect is eliminated; status, resume state, and log counts strictly agree. *(Verified by code reading and test execution)*.

2. **Atomic Single-Writer `DECISION.json` & Gate Liveness**:
   - Concurrency is managed via `os.open(lock, os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_WRONLY)` on [`DECISION.lock`](file:///home/u24/papers/mcrl-leo-handover-cf3/scripts/run_cf3_pilot.py#L285-L298). Temp files are PID-unique (`DECISION.json.{os.getpid()}.tmp`) and replaced atomically.
   - The decision records code commit, calibration SHA, TLE SHA, A1 seed values, random reference, and gate episode within `gate_fingerprint`. Stale decisions from prior runs fail closed with `SystemExit`.
   - If an A1 run dies before publishing, waiting processes time out after `gate_timeout_s` and raise [`GateUnavailable`](file:///home/u24/papers/mcrl-leo-handover-cf3/scripts/run_cf3_pilot.py#L51-L54) (subclass of `RuntimeError`), which writes `status="failed"` and re-raises with a non-zero exit code. In [`cf3_launch.py:136-145`](file:///home/u24/papers/mcrl-leo-handover-cf3/scripts/cf3_launch.py#L136-L145), `real_fail` requires `DECISION.json` with `pass: False`, so missing decisions are planned as `"resume"`, never `"finished"`. *(Verified by code reading and test execution)*.

3. **Cryptographic Manifest & Fail-Closed Guards**:
   - [`code_manifest()`](file:///home/u24/papers/mcrl-leo-handover-cf3/scripts/cf3_common.py#L168-L182) hashes all 11 core files (`cf_ratio.py`, `cf_sources.py`, `modqn.py`, `run_cf3_pilot.py`, `cf3_common.py`, `cf3_launch.py`, `cf3_pools.py`, and Declaration + Amendments 1–3) plus the recursive `src/` tree and Git commit.
   - [`RUN-MANIFEST.json`](file:///home/u24/papers/mcrl-leo-handover-cf3/scripts/cf3_launch.py#L109-L126) binds code identity, calibration SHA, TLE root, and all pool file hashes. Launch and resume verify against this manifest and abort immediately on mismatch. *(Verified by code reading)*.

4. **Real Driver Process-Level Testing**:
   - [`cf3_proctest.py`](file:///home/u24/papers/mcrl-leo-handover-cf3/scripts/cf3_proctest.py#L1-L127) exercises the actual driver under `systemd-run --user --scope`. T1 confirms interrupted/resumed runs produce bit-identical Q-networks (`torch.equal`) and identical RNG progression to uninterrupted runs. T2 confirms forced gate failure cleanly terminates A1 runs at episode 2 with `status: "stopped-learning-check"`. *(Verified by code reading and unit tests)*.

5. **Process Liveness & Batch Scope**:
   - [`is_live()`](file:///home/u24/papers/mcrl-leo-handover-cf3/scripts/cf3_launch.py#L49-L65) checks `/proc/{pid}/cmdline` and `/proc/{pid}/cwd` to prevent PID reuse issues. Launched processes are verified alive 10 seconds post-launch; startup failures fail loudly.
